+## Story Q8 — Self-Healing: Question Budget + Cache + Stuck-Agent Heuristics + needs_info TTL (medium, 1.5 days)
+
+**Goal:** make the fleet stop burning tokens on stuck agents and looping questions. Combined with Q7 (knowledge cache), this is the throughput unlock.
+
+**Files added:**
+- `tech_dev_agents/ops_console/services/self_healing.py` — heuristic detectors.
+- Migration extension to Q3 policy table (new failure classes) + budget config table.
+- Background tasks added to ops-console: `dispatch_stuck_agent_watcher` (90s), `dispatch_needs_info_ttl` (5 min, already specified in Q3 above).
+
+**New failure classes (added to Q3 policy):**
+
+| Class | Retryable | Max | Cooldown | Lane |
+|-------|-----------|-----|----------|------|
+| `agent_stuck_question_budget_exceeded` | FALSE | 0 | 0 | attention_queue |
+| `agent_repetition` | FALSE | 0 | 0 | attention_queue |
+| `phase_overrun` | FALSE | 0 | 0 | attention_queue |
+| `agent_flapping` | FALSE | 0 | 0 | attention_queue |
+| `dependency_unresolved_7d` | FALSE | 0 | 0 | dead_letter |
+
+**Budget config:**
+
+```sql
+CREATE TABLE dispatch_question_budget (
+    scope         TEXT PRIMARY KEY,        -- small | medium | large | epic
+    max_questions INT NOT NULL,
+    max_per_phase INT NOT NULL
+);
+INSERT INTO dispatch_question_budget VALUES
+    ('small',  2, 1),
+    ('medium', 3, 2),
+    ('large',  5, 2),
+    ('epic',   8, 3);
+```
+
+**Pre-question budget enforcement** (in `/api/dispatch/v2/transition` when event_type='needs_info'):
+1. Count prior `needs_info` events for this job; if `>= max_questions`, reject with 409 and emit `failed` with class `agent_stuck_question_budget_exceeded`.
+2. Otherwise allow needs_info but log used budget in event_data.
+
+**Stuck-agent detectors** (`dispatch_stuck_agent_watcher`, runs every 90s):
+
+| Heuristic | Detection | Action |
+|-----------|-----------|--------|
+| **Idle-no-progress** | Lease alive, heartbeat alive, but git working-tree SHA unchanged for >20 min (poller reports SHA every heartbeat) | Release lease, emit `failed` with class `agent_repetition` |
+| **Same-commit-loop** | Same commit SHA produced ≥3 times across phase retries | Release lease, emit `failed` with class `agent_repetition` |
+| **Phase-time-budget** | Phase duration > 2× scope-typical (small=20min, medium=60min, large=120min) | Release lease, emit `failed` with class `phase_overrun` |
+| **Test-flap** | RED → GREEN → RED → GREEN within 10 min, no commit progress | Release lease, emit `failed` with class `agent_flapping` |
+
+**Heartbeat protocol extension:** poller's heartbeat now includes `{git_head_sha, current_phase, phase_started_at, last_test_status}`. Server stores in `dispatch_leases.heartbeat_data jsonb`. Watcher reads this jsonb to evaluate heuristics.
+
+**Acceptance criteria (Q8):**
+- AC1: Question budget enforced server-side; replay test (story with 3 sequential needs_info on `scope=small`, max=2) produces 1 `agent_stuck_question_budget_exceeded` failure.
+- AC2: Idle-no-progress detector fires within 90s of git_head_sha staying constant for 20 min.
+- AC3: Same-commit-loop detector fires after 3 identical SHAs.
+- AC4: Phase-time-budget detector fires when phase duration exceeds 2× scope baseline.
+- AC5: Test-flap detector requires structured `last_test_status` from poller heartbeats; fires on the documented pattern.
+- AC6: All Q8 detectors emit `failed` events with proper `failure_class` and `failure_reason` (DB constraint enforced).
+- AC7: needs_info TTL (24h → attention_queue) implemented per Q3 spec.
+- AC8: Combined with Q7: replay 2026-04-30 11-similar-needs_info incident; expected outcome — first question pauses, cluster detection fires after 3rd, remaining 8 stories receive cluster answer automatically and resume. Zero of the 11 burn full retry budget.
