+# Overwatch Runbook — Mark + Morris
+
+> Operating model for keeping the dispatch fleet healthy on an ongoing basis. Not the freeze checklist (that's in `implementation-plan.md`). This runbook applies **after** the 7-day freeze, regardless of whether queue v2 ships.
+
+## Roles
+
+### Mark — Overwatch Lead (human)
+Sets priorities, makes vetoes, owns knowledge-layer sign-off, decides escalations Morris can't auto-resolve.
+
+### Morris — Overwatch Operator (manager-role agent)
+Routine operational interventions. Daily/hourly cadence. Self-runs on cron; escalates when policy demands it.
+
+### Dan / Daisy / Devon / Derrick — Developer agents
+Claim and execute stories. Do not perform overwatch. May be paused by Morris, may be force-released by either Mark or Morris.
+
+---
+
+## Cadences
+
+### Morris — hourly
+- **Fleet vigilance sweep** (existing 16-check skill).
+- **Stale-lease watchdog**: any lease where `expires_at < now() - 5min` and no recent heartbeat → release + emit `released` event with reason `stale_lease`.
+- **Quarantine review**: any quarantined job whose underlying cause has cleared (e.g., dependency satisfied, 409 storm subsided) → emit `requeued` event.
+
+### Morris — daily (08:00 ET)
+- **Queue Health Brief**, posted to Teams ops channel:
+  - Per-lane counts (work_queue, in_progress, in_review, human_queue, attention_queue, terminal-completed-24h, terminal-failed-24h).
+  - Top 5 jobs by lease age (in_progress).
+  - Top 5 jobs by needs_info age (human_queue).
+  - Failure-class distribution (last 24h) with deltas vs. 7-day baseline.
+  - Knowledge-layer hit rate (Q7 metric: `% of stories where context-load injected ≥1 page from gc-knowledgebase`).
+  - Question-budget exhaustion count (Q8 metric).
+- **Knowledge-layer ingest curation**: review yesterday's `tech-gc-knowledgebase/scratch/` adds; auto-promote ones tagged "high-confidence", flag the rest for Mark.
+
+### Morris — weekly (Monday 08:00 ET)
+- **Trend report**: 7-day rolling deltas on every SLO metric. Anything trending wrong → flag.
+- **Stuck-story sweep**: any job in `attention_queue` for >7 days → DM Mark with summary.
+- **Knowledge-layer freshness audit**: any `wiki/` page older than 90 days that's been referenced ≥10 times → flag for review (it's load-bearing and aging).
+
+### Mark — weekly (Friday 16:00 ET, ~30 min)
+- **Fleet health review**: read the week's Queue Health Briefs; sign off on Morris's curation queue; veto/approve any pending epic decisions.
+- **Knowledge-layer curation**: walk through `scratch/` pages Morris flagged; promote, edit, or reject.
+- **Cost burn review**: per-failure-class token spend vs. ceiling (see thresholds below). Adjust ceilings if the policy is wrong.
+
+### Mark — monthly
+- **Dispatch reliability retro**: standalone retro on the dispatch surface. Inputs: Morris's monthly trend; failure-class top-3; knowledge-layer hit-rate trend; PR-rework rate. Output: 1-3 hardening proposals (or "no action needed").
+- **Knowledge-layer signal review**: which `wiki/` pages got referenced most? Which got referenced zero times? Prune dead pages.
+
+### Mark — quarterly
+- **Architecture review**: do the v2 primitives still fit? Are there new failure classes Q3's policy table doesn't cover? Has `dispatch_v2_events` schema accumulated drift? File one epic if needed; otherwise no-op.
+
+---
+
+## Failure-Class Escalation Matrix
+
+| Class | Auto-handled by Morris | Mark involvement |
+|-------|------------------------|-------------------|
+| `argparse_reject` | dead-letter | only if class spikes (signal of deploy break) |
+| `rate_limited` | quarantine + auto-requeue when rate-limit window clears (per Q3 policy) | only if persistent >24h |
+| `branch_setup_failed` | retry per policy; if 3x fail, attention | Mark decides if branch convention drift |
+| `needs_info_unanswered` (post-24h TTL) | attention | Mark answers via `/answer-needs-info` |
+| `sdk_died_silent` | retry per policy | only if cost ceiling breached |
+| `phase_runner_crash` | retry per policy | only if class spikes |
+| `code_test_red` | attention | Mark or rework dispatch |
+| `adversarial_block` | attention | Mark resolves the security/scope concern |
+| `dependency_missing` | quarantine; watcher requeues when dep clears | only if `dependency_unresolved_7d` fires |
+| `agent_stuck_question_budget_exceeded` (NEW Q8) | attention | Mark decides: rescope or unblock |
+| `agent_repetition` (NEW Q8) | attention | Mark decides: kill story or guide |
+| `phase_overrun` (NEW Q8) | attention | Mark decides: increase budget or split |
+| `agent_flapping` (NEW Q8) | attention | Mark decides: bug in agent or in test |
+| `dependency_unresolved_7d` (NEW Q3) | dead-letter | Mark must reconfirm dep or cancel |
+| `unknown` | attention | Mark classifies; Morris updates Q3 policy table |
+
+**Rule:** Morris never moves a job to `dead_letter` without Mark's prior approval, except for the classes explicitly marked `dead_letter` in the policy table. Auto-dead-letter is reserved for deterministic non-retryables (argparse_reject) and TTL-expired (`dependency_unresolved_7d`).
+
+---
+
+## Cost-Burn Ceilings Per Failure Class
+
+A class breaching its ceiling = pause that class's auto-retry, alert Mark.
+
+| Class | Per-story ceiling | Per-day fleet ceiling | If breached |
+|-------|---------------------|------------------------|-------------|
+| `rate_limited` | $0 (released, not retried with cost) | n/a | n/a |
+| `branch_setup_failed` | $1 (3 retries × ~$0.30) | $5 | pause class, alert Mark |
+| `sdk_died_silent` | $5 | $20 | pause class, alert Mark |
+| `phase_runner_crash` | $5 | $20 | pause class, alert Mark |
+| `code_test_red` | n/a (no retry) | n/a | n/a — Mark/rework decides |
+| `dependency_missing` | $0 (quarantined) | n/a | n/a |
+| All other classes | n/a (attention or dead-letter, no retry) | n/a | n/a |
+
+Ceilings are enforced by `dispatch_cost_guard` (background job, runs every 10 min) reading event_data and Foundry billing; emits `paused` event with reason `cost_ceiling_breached` when fired.
+
+---
+
+## When to Break the Freeze (precommitted criteria)
+
+The freeze period (Decision Gate, 7 days) has a non-negotiable rule: no dispatch-surface changes. But **legitimate emergencies** can require a break. To prevent ad-hoc judgment calls, here are the precommitted criteria:
+
+**Break the freeze ONLY if:**
+1. Production data corruption is occurring (e.g., `dispatch_items` row state inconsistent with reality, agent runtime mutations leaking).
+2. Fleet is fully down (>3 of 4 agents offline >30 min) AND root cause is in a frozen file.
+3. Cost burn is ≥3× normal AND root cause is in a frozen file.
+4. A security incident requires it (CVE, leaked credential, unauthorized access).
+
+**Do NOT break the freeze for:**
+- "An agent got stuck on STORY-X" → Morris quarantines and force-releases; story waits.
+- "We have a better idea about the queue" → write it down for the post-freeze retro.
+- "The dashboard shows a glitch" → file a story for after the freeze.
+- "A new story type doesn't fit the current model" → defer dispatch of that story type for 7 days.
+
+**Break protocol:**
+1. Morris drafts impact note: symptom, affected stories, expected risk, rollback path.
+2. Mark approves in writing (Teams thread) with explicit "FREEZE-BREAK APPROVED" tag.
+3. Morris executes. Bounded change set. Validation signal expected within 30 min.
+4. Logged in `freeze-ledger.md` for the day-7 decision context.
+
+---
+
+## Knowledge-Layer Governance
+
+`tech-gc-knowledgebase` is the fleet's long-term memory. Governance prevents it from becoming a graveyard or a hallucination farm.
+
+### Promotion rules (`scratch/` → `wiki/`)
+- **Auto-promote** (Morris, no Mark approval): pages that are pure mechanical extracts (Monday.com board snapshots, NetSuite Item Master changes, GitHub repo metadata). Tagged `auto:mechanical`.
+- **Mark-approval required**: pages that encode decisions, business rules, anti-patterns, or architectural choices. Tagged `human:judgment`.
+- **Never auto-promoted**: pages with PII, confidential business plans, or pages that disagree with an existing `wiki/` page (must be reconciled).
+
+### Pruning rules
+- Pages not referenced in 180 days AND not in the "evergreen" list (org chart, SDLC process, etc.) → flagged by Morris's weekly audit. Mark decides keep/prune.
+- Pages with a successor (newer page covers same topic) → previous page archived to `wiki/_archive/{date}/` with cross-link.
+
+### Citation discipline
+- When agents inject a knowledgebase page into a prompt, they must cite it in the resulting deliverable: `[per knowledgebase: wiki/<path>]`.
+- Citations are extracted into a per-story `knowledge_used.md` for audit.
+- Pages with zero citations after 90 days = candidates for pruning.
+
+### Conflict resolution
+- If two pages disagree on the same fact, Morris flags. Mark decides which is authoritative; loser is archived.
+- An agent that finds contradictions in its injected context must surface them in `QUESTION.md` (this is one of the few legitimate question types).
+
+---
+
