+# EPIC-Queue-v2 — Lease + Log + Contract
+
+**Frontend:** false (backend epic; minor dashboard adapter in Story 4)
+
+## Overview
+| Field | Value |
+|-------|-------|
+| Mode | feature_update |
+| Scope | epic |
+| Feature Name | Dispatch queue v2 — lease-based claim, event-sourced state, versioned contract |
+| Phase Path | Epic: 1 → decompose → per-story SDLC → [E2E gate] → repeat → Retrospective → Done |
+| Repo | tech-dev-agents |
+| Estimated effort | ~10 working days (2 calendar weeks with soak) |
+| Owner | Mark (architect); decomposed stories assigned per fleet capacity |
+
+## Problem Statement
+
+The dispatch queue has produced ~20 reactive stories in the last 2 weeks (STORY-507, 531, 538, 552, 700, 701, 702, 723, 725, 740, 741, 762, 763, 769, 791, 795, 798, 799, 800, 801, 802) and three more dispatch-fix commits in the last 24 hours (`b8991bb`, `6307d6b`, `49eb72e`). Each fix is correct in isolation. The pattern is the bug.
+
+**Root cause (as diagnosed in [diagnosis.md](./diagnosis.md)):** the queue is a row-store with mutating status + scattered policy. There is no canonical event log, no lease primitive, and no producer/consumer contract version. Five concrete consequences keep producing incidents:
+
+1. **D1 — State lives in a single mutable row, not in a log.** `dispatch_items` has 20+ columns and grows every story. `dispatch_events` exists (STORY-700) but is a side-effect emit after row mutation, not the source of truth.
+2. **D2 — There is no lease, only a status flag.** Every recovery path (force_release, has_active_claim, phantom-claim guard, heartbeat watchdog) re-derives ownership from row state.
+3. **D3 — Selection (`/dispatch/next`) and locking (`/dispatch/claim/{id}`) are decoupled across two HTTP calls.** Race window between them; gates duplicated in both endpoints because the retry path bypasses `/next`.
+4. **D4 — Policy is scattered.** Dependency parsing, role gating, rate-limit detection, failure classification, phantom-claim guard, lane re-bucketing — each lives in a different file (poller, route, db_service, migrations).
+5. **D5 — No producer/consumer protocol contract.** `try/except TypeError` runtime fallbacks for older `db_service` signatures; in-place edits of migration 008; bootstrap migration 001 made re-entrant after the fact.
+
+## Target User
+
+**Primary:** dispatch poller fleet (Dan, Daisy, Devon, Derrick), ops-console route layer, Morris (manager-role agent).
+**Secondary:** Mark (operator who reads the queue dashboard and answers `needs_info`).
+
+**Today:** every dispatch incident produces a reactive patch on top of an architecture that doesn't have the right primitives. Queue success rate ~34% (per Morris fleet assessment 2026-04-22). 11 silent failures with `failure_reason=NULL` on 2026-04-29. Head-of-line blockage outage 2026-04-30. 409 thrash incidents recurring.
+
+**After this epic:** atomic claim-next with a lease token. Event log is the source of truth; row state is a derived projection. Worker version contract enforced server-side. Failure classification + retry policy centralized. Lanes are queries, not columns.
+
+## Success Criteria (Epic-level)
+
+**Plumbing (queue v2 stories Q1-Q6):**
+- **SC-1 — Zero 409 claim loops** for 7 consecutive days post-cutover (same `(story_id, repo)` getting >5 409s in 2 minutes).
+- **SC-2 — Head-of-line age < 5 minutes** while eligible jobs exist (measured server-side).
+- **SC-3 — 100% of fail events carry `failure_class` and `failure_reason`** (DB-enforced via trigger on `dispatch_v2_events.event_data`).
+- **SC-4 — Zero runtime version shims** in poller or route. Worker version mismatch returns structured 426; poller refuses to start on protocol mismatch.
+- **SC-5 — State auditability:** "what was the state of STORY-X at 14:32 UTC" answerable from the event log alone, no row-state archaeology.
+- **SC-6 — Lane separation is a query, not a column.** `needs_info` overload (human Q&A vs. ops attention) is gone; distinguished by `event_data.kind` at write time.
+- **SC-7 — Single deploy artifact.** Route + migrations + protocol-version manifest ship together; partial deploys are refused by the route on startup.
+- **SC-8 — Redispatch correctness:** zero duplicate active jobs per PR/branch correlation key for 7 soak days; parent-state guard enforced; lineage endpoint live.
+
+**Cognition (Q7 knowledge layer + Q8 self-healing):**
+- **SC-9 — Knowledge-layer hit rate ≥60%:** at least 60% of stories have ≥1 gc-knowledgebase page injected at Phase 1 start (`knowledge_citations` populated).
+- **SC-10 — Question budget enforced:** per-scope question caps active; a story exceeding budget moves to `attention_queue` automatically with `agent_stuck_question_budget_exceeded`.
+- **SC-11 — Self-healing detectors live:** stuck-agent watcher fires on idle-no-progress, same-commit-loop, phase-overrun, agent-flapping. Replay of 2026-04-30 11-similar-needs_info incident shows ≤2 stories burning full retry budget (vs. all 11 today).
+- **SC-12 — Cluster-answer auto-resume:** when ≥3 needs_info questions cluster (Jaccard ≥0.4), a single answer auto-resumes the cluster.
+
+**Apprenticeship (Q9 declining overwatch):**
+- **SC-13 — Mark touch rate trending down:** quarterly comparison shows Mark's required-touch count per week declining or flat (never rising for >3 quarters in a row).
+- **SC-14 — Apprenticeship loop active:** weekly proposer surfaces ≥1 candidate rule when ≥3 same-input-hash decisions exist; approved rules execute auto and log overrides; auto-disable on override-rate >10%.
+
+## Non-Goals
+
+- Rebuilding the dispatch poller end-to-end. Only the claim path changes.
+- Replacing Postgres or introducing a message broker (Redis, RabbitMQ). The DB is fine; the schema is wrong.
+- Rewriting dispatch skill transport semantics. Producer-side transport stays the same; only enqueue-time metadata normalization for v2 (for example dependency extraction into `dispatch_dependencies`) is in scope.
+- Rewriting the dashboard. Story 4 ships a thin adapter so existing TypeScript types continue to work.
+
+## Decomposition (9 stories — plumbing + cognition + apprenticeship)
+
+| Story | Title | Scope | Effort |
+|-------|-------|-------|--------|
+| STORY-Q1 | `dispatch_jobs` schema + `dispatch_v2_events` as source of truth + projection table | medium | 2 days |
+| STORY-Q2 | Atomic `claim-next` + lease token + worker version contract + redispatch contract (R1.1–R1.5 + RT1–RT8) | medium | 2 days |
+| STORY-Q3 | Centralized retry/failure policy + DLQ + dependency watcher + needs_info TTL | small | 1 day |
+| STORY-Q4 | Lane derivation in projection + dashboard adapter | small | 0.5 day |
+| STORY-Q5 | Cutover (poller v2 deploy → route flip → 7-day soak) | medium | 1 day + 7 day soak |
+| STORY-Q6 | Single deploy artifact + protocol-version manifest + partial-deploy rejection | small | 1 day |
+| **STORY-Q7** | **Knowledge layer — gc-knowledgebase as agent memory (read at story-start, write at story-complete, dedupe via cache)** | **medium** | **2 days** |
+| **STORY-Q8** | **Self-healing — question budget + cache + stuck-agent heuristics + needs_info TTL** | **medium** | **1.5 days** |
+| **STORY-Q9** | **Declining overwatch — apprenticeship loop (decisions log, pattern proposer, auto-rules with override guards, touch-rate trend)** | **medium** | **1.5 days** |
+
+**Total:** ~12.5 dev days + 7-day soak. Phase 0 ("stop the bleed", 0.5 day) precedes Q1.
+
+**Sequencing:** Phase 0 → Decision Gate (7-day freeze) → if FAIL: Q1 → Q2 → (Q3 ‖ Q4 ‖ Q6 ‖ Q7 ‖ Q8 ‖ Q9) → Q5 cutover + soak. If PASS: cancel Q1-Q6; ship Q7+Q8+Q9 standalone (they're independently valuable). Q7 and Q8 ship together (cache-driven prevention works only with the knowledge layer present). Q9 can ship anytime after Q1's `dispatch_v2_events` exists (it logs decisions there).
+
+**Documents in this epic folder:**
+- [seed.md](./seed.md) — this file (epic intro, success criteria, decomposition)
+- [diagnosis.md](./diagnosis.md) — root-cause analysis of the v1 queue's structural defects (D1-D5)
+- [architecture.md](./architecture.md) — master reference: components, data flow, state machine, contracts, risks, tradeoffs
+- [implementation-plan.md](./implementation-plan.md) — per-story specs, schemas, endpoints, ACs, cutover sequence
+- [review.md](./review.md) — round-2 deep evaluation: gaps, fixes (this file is what added Q7/Q8/Q9)
+- [overwatch-runbook.md](./overwatch-runbook.md) — ongoing operating model: cadences, escalation matrix, declining-overwatch ladder
+
+## Constraints
+
+| Constraint | Value |
+|------------|-------|
+| Budget | 1 senior engineer (likely Mark + Dan/Devon for individual stories) |
+| Timeline | 10 working days end-to-end; 7-day soak before declaring done |
+| Scale | ~200 dispatch_items rows steady-state; spike to ~500 during epic decompositions |
+| Risk | Cutover is the highest-risk step; freeze-first alternative documented in adversarial review |
+| Coexistence | v2 schema coexists with v1 during cutover window only; no long-term dual-write |
+
+## Decision Gate Before Decomposition
+
+**This epic only ships if a 7-day dispatch-surface freeze fails to stabilize the SLO.** Per the adversarial review (A10), the strongest counter to v2 is that the bug may be *policy churn*, not architecture. Before committing to the epic:
+
+1. Ship Phase 0 (SLO dashboard + auto-quarantine, ~0.5 day).
+2. Freeze all dispatch-route, poller, and migration changes for 7 days.
+3. If 409-rate, head-of-line-age, and `failure_reason`-null rate all flatten under freeze → cancel the epic; write up findings; tighten policy-change governance instead.
+4. If SLO stays red under freeze → proceed with Story Q1.
+
+This gate is non-negotiable. We have spent two weeks shipping reactive fixes; one week of disciplined non-action is cheap insurance against rebuilding something that wasn't broken at the layer we're rebuilding.
